    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is about whether the completed trip deviated from the route shown at booking, and on the record the answer is no within the meaning of the policy, so the fare as charged stands and nothing is refunded.\n\nTHE THRESHOLD. POL-RD-01 makes the GPS trace the governing measurement and sets two tests that must BOTH pass: the excess must be greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of the booking-time optimal. The trace (EV-GPS-09112, weight 1.0) records trace_distance_km of 11.5 km; the booking-time optimal on the trip record (EV-TRIP-09112, weight 1.0) is 10.0 km. The excess is 1.5 km, which clears the 0.8 km absolute limb but is 15.0% of optimal, short of the 20% limb. Because one establishment test fails, POL-RD-01 states there is no deviation and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The rider's submission that the trip was '1.5 km longer' is factually right and is accepted on the measurement; it does not clear the policy threshold, and that is the ground of this ruling.\n\nWHAT DOES NOT MOVE IT. (1) The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 133 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum inter-fix gap 0.0 s, admissibility COMPLETE at weight 1.0. POL-RD-07 limbs (a)–(c) are not engaged, the 1.5 km is not a sampling artefact, and the no-corroboration escalation in POL-RD-10(3) is not triggered. Both advocates' claims on this point are accepted. (2) The baseline is 10.0 km and nothing shifts it: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null with amended_optimal_distance_km null, so POL-RD-05 has no re-quote to apply, and vehicle_type is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-12's pooled matched-itinerary baseline does not apply. (3) POL-RD-04 gives the driver no exoneration and takes nothing from the rider either: the only chat message (EV-CHAT-09112) is the rider's own mid-trip remark, it names no place or road and carries a null waypoint_hint, so the corroboration test cannot be run on this record. (4) The one refund route that survives a failed POL-RD-01 test — billing integrity under POL-RD-09(4) — is closed: no ERP gantry is charged (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00) and no airport surcharge is applied on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport. (5) POL-RD-06 is not engaged: 1.5 km / 15.0% is neither greater than 50% nor greater than 8.0 km, so it is not a MATERIAL deviation, and the driver's citable 90-day counters (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 610) show no pattern in any event.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. The rider's arithmetic claim (recomputed_fare 17.70, refund 1.69 rounded up to 1.70, PARTIAL_REFUND) is accepted as arithmetic but not reached, because it is conditional on a deviation being established and none is. The rider's alternative request — that the contested SGD 1.69 be held for a human reviewer under POL-RD-10 rather than left standing — is not granted. A request is not a trigger: POL-RD-01's own terms direct NO_ACTION where a threshold limb fails, and no enumerated POL-RD-10 trigger fires. Trace not impaired (no (3)); trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown and the trace's first fix matches started_at, so no (2); no timestamp conflict, no (4); no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact, because no closure or other exoneration was asserted and the absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09112-01 (weight 0.0) merely confirms POL-RD-03 has nothing to run on, so no (5); no charge line lacks a counterpart, no (8); the refund does not exceed SGD 150.00 or charged_total, no (6); and this is not two sides with contradictory evidence of comparable strength — the rider herself concedes the threshold is not met, no (7). The driver's counter-statement ('ordinary through roads, no additional stop') carries no weight multiplier and no clause in this category names a counterparty statement as its test, so it neither adds nor detracts; the outcome does not depend on it. The profile fields the rider correctly flagged as context-only (prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld) were not used as a ground of decision by either side, and POL-GEN-01 forbids it.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND OUTCOME. The deciding facts — the trace distance and the booking-time optimal — are carried by artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-GPS-09112, EV-TRIP-09112), so confidence is not capped below the platform floor and no escalation arises under POL-GEN-02 or POL-RD-10(1). EV-ADVIS-09112-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and can carry no fact; its absence is noted and changes nothing, since the threshold fails on the unimpaired trace regardless. Ruling: NO_ACTION. fare_breakdown.payment_status (CHARGED) and refund_issued_sgd (0.00) are left as they are; the contested SGD 1.69 is neither refunded nor held."
